1
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:08,633
To be honest...

2
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:11,011
[soft dramatic music playing]

3
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,307
I've always...

4
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:22,648
always...

5
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:30,530
- [car horn blares]
- [grunts]

6
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:31,782
According to Article 224
of the Criminal Code,

7
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:33,407
kissing someone
without consent...

8
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:34,535
What are you doing,
Chao Yi-hsuan?

9
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:36,453
...is an offense
of forcible indecency.

10
00:00:39,206 --> 00:00:40,581
Am I disturbing you, Boss?

11
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:42,500
Is she kissing you
with your consent?

12
00:00:42,501 --> 00:00:44,336
[whimsical music playing]

13
00:00:45,837 --> 00:00:47,713
I'm sober now.

14
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:50,842
- So annoying.
- It's Yu-li's birthday.

15
00:00:51,093 --> 00:00:52,678
Our boss has to be there.

16
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:57,015
But she's drunk.
I'll take her home.

17
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,351
- No, I'll go by myself.
- No, I'll call her a taxi.

18
00:01:04,231 --> 00:01:05,274
Are you sure?

19
00:01:07,109 --> 00:01:08,151
Yeah.

20
00:01:09,695 --> 00:01:11,697
I'm sober now.
I'll go home by myself.

21
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:14,408
[music continues]

22
00:01:23,417 --> 00:01:24,543
Be safe!

23
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:35,721
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can
Find sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

24
00:01:35,846 --> 00:01:40,391
[singing in Mandarin]

25
00:01:40,392 --> 00:01:42,476
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

26
00:01:42,477 --> 00:01:44,770
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

27
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:46,857
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

28
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:49,233
[singing in Mandarin]

29
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:52,863
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

30
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:56,199
[singing in Mandarin]

31
00:02:01,163 --> 00:02:04,207
- [disco music playing]
- [loud chatter]

32
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:11,590
[man] Hey, pal.

33
00:02:12,591 --> 00:02:14,885
That girl over there
has been looking at you.

34
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:19,848
The one in a brown dress.

35
00:02:24,603 --> 00:02:25,854
Cool!

36
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:31,692
- [Chien-yuan] Hey.
- Hey.

37
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:35,322
Would you like to come with me
for a game of pool?

38
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:37,949
- [woman] I'll think about it.
- Huh?

39
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,451
I'll think about it.

40
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:47,501
Cool!

41
00:02:47,626 --> 00:02:49,669
I'll order a couple
of drinks for you.

42
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:52,672
[people cheering]

43
00:02:52,673 --> 00:02:55,467
[music continues]

44
00:03:00,472 --> 00:03:01,723
What's wrong with you?

45
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:06,144
- I want you
to stay away from her.
- Don't touch me!

46
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:07,312
[man] What?

47
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:10,648
- Don't push me!
- [man] What?

48
00:03:10,649 --> 00:03:11,650
[Chien-yuan] Don't push me!

49
00:03:11,775 --> 00:03:13,860
- [man] What?
- Damn you!

50
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:17,488
Can't you hear me?
I told you not to touch me.

51
00:03:17,489 --> 00:03:19,658
Damn it!
Do you not understand?

52
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:21,742
Don't you know who I am?

53
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:23,495
Damn! Bastard!

54
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,205
<i>Don't you know who I am?</i>

55
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:27,708
- [phone dings]
- Do you know who this is?

56
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:28,959
CHANG XIN'S STOCK PRICE
IS PLUMMETING.

57
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:30,459
Damn you!

58
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,585
UNBELIEVABLE!
TYPICAL TRUST FUND BABY.

59
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:33,922
[cell phone dings]

60
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:39,885
[Chien-yuan]
Son of a bitch! Damn!

61
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:40,845
Damn!

62
00:03:40,846 --> 00:03:42,931
[upbeat music playing]

63
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:45,933
QUEEN: MISSION COMPLETED!
LOVE YOU.

64
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:47,768
A: NO PROBLEM. MY FRIEND KNEW
CHANG CHIEN-YUAN WOULD BE THERE.

65
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:48,936
A: DAMN! THAT'S SO LOW,
BUYING ONE-STAR REVIEWS.

66
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:50,605
- LALA: COOL!
- PETER: KILL THEM.

67
00:03:50,981 --> 00:03:53,692
QUEEN: I OWE YOU ONE!
NEXT TIME YOU COME TO THE SHOP,
IT'S ON ME.

68
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:04,995
You're swimming too hard.

69
00:04:08,749 --> 00:04:11,543
Where's your phone?
Have you seen the news?

70
00:04:12,544 --> 00:04:14,545
The headline is...

71
00:04:14,546 --> 00:04:17,798
"Chang Xin Heir
Fights in Nightclub:

72
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:20,302
Path of Succession
Far Out of Reach."

73
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:22,804
Damn!

74
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:26,766
Those journalists...

75
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:28,477
have nothing better to do.

76
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:31,980
You're getting roasted online.

77
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:33,732
Damn!

78
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:36,776
Never mind those idiots.

79
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:39,362
"I heard he has
many dirty tricks
and always slings mud."

80
00:04:39,488 --> 00:04:41,572
"He's that rich
and still bullying
a small restaurant?"

81
00:04:41,573 --> 00:04:42,574
Hey.

82
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:52,625
Pal, I've found
something about this wave
of online attacks,

83
00:04:52,626 --> 00:04:54,961
but I'm not sure
if I should tell you.

84
00:04:57,964 --> 00:04:59,423
Damn! Tell me now.

85
00:04:59,424 --> 00:05:00,926
Stop playing tricks.

86
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:07,306
Those influencers attacking you
have one thing in common.

87
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:08,433
What?

88
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:11,478
They're all friends
of the Queen of Reviews.

89
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:18,068
Damn!

90
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:19,152
JIN LAI HAO

91
00:05:22,614 --> 00:05:23,740
[Chien-yuan] Hey!

92
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:26,618
Hey!

93
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:29,287
You. Yeah, you.

94
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:30,997
Damn it! You did it, right?

95
00:05:31,873 --> 00:05:33,833
What have I done?

96
00:05:33,834 --> 00:05:34,918
Don't play dumb.

97
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:37,670
Do you know that's defamation?

98
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:39,631
That is rich.
Do you own the courthouse?

99
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:41,800
What's that got to do with this?

100
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:43,844
I meant that video.

101
00:05:43,969 --> 00:05:44,970
Here's some advice...

102
00:05:45,095 --> 00:05:46,470
[dramatic music playing]

103
00:05:46,471 --> 00:05:48,682
- What?
- To protect myself.

104
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:51,768
I was stopped
by a stranger on the street,
and he was a jerk.

105
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:53,311
I'm so scared.

106
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:55,062
I'm not doing anything to you.

107
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:57,649
I just want you
to delete the video.

108
00:05:57,774 --> 00:06:01,527
It's fine if you don't.
I'll take legal action.
That's all.

109
00:06:01,528 --> 00:06:03,654
So arrogant.
You sue people for everything?

110
00:06:03,655 --> 00:06:05,990
Does your company
have 500 legal specialists?

111
00:06:05,991 --> 00:06:07,533
Did you see that?

112
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:08,785
You all saw that, right?

113
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:11,036
This is the heir of Chang Xin.

114
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:13,122
Can the heir
of Chang Xin do that?

115
00:06:13,123 --> 00:06:15,000
Stopping a random girl
on the street?

116
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:16,751
Come on.

117
00:06:17,002 --> 00:06:18,502
Can the heir of Chang Xin
harass a girl on the street?

118
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:20,171
- Come on. Stop it.
- I often eat at Chang Xin.

119
00:06:20,422 --> 00:06:22,173
- Stop filming.
- Don't touch me.

120
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:24,008
If I were your dad,
you'd never be my successor.

121
00:06:24,009 --> 00:06:25,510
You're so embarrassing.

122
00:06:27,429 --> 00:06:28,763
What are you talking about?

123
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:32,517
Is this how you treat customers
at Chang Xin?

124
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:33,685
Shut up!

125
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:35,687
- [Yi-hsuan] See?
- [woman] He's hitting her.

126
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:36,770
[Yi-hsuan] That's so weak!

127
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:38,523
Don't you work out?

128
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:39,857
Take a video.

129
00:06:39,858 --> 00:06:40,859
Do it again.

130
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:42,568
I've got you on video.

131
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:43,904
I'll post it tonight.

132
00:06:44,029 --> 00:06:45,530
- Want me to do it again?
- I'll post it later.

133
00:06:49,409 --> 00:06:51,077
- What are you doing?
- Damn you!

134
00:06:51,202 --> 00:06:52,579
Let go, Chou Lu-yung!

135
00:06:52,704 --> 00:06:54,038
What are you doing?

136
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:55,915
None of your business!
Trying to play the hero?

137
00:06:55,916 --> 00:06:56,875
Stop it!

138
00:06:58,668 --> 00:07:00,587
There are many people around.
Are you sure you want
to do this?

139
00:07:00,712 --> 00:07:03,465
[soft tense music playing]

140
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,556
Freaking bastards.

141
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:15,894
Good riddance.
See you online tonight.

142
00:07:17,896 --> 00:07:21,608
Got it. Got it.
Chang Chien-yuan is dead! Look!

143
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:24,903
Your cheek is swollen.

144
00:07:26,488 --> 00:07:27,614
I'm fine.

145
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:30,742
Are you alright?

146
00:07:32,953 --> 00:07:35,538
I think it slightly hurts.

147
00:07:37,707 --> 00:07:39,918
Don't do something
so dangerous again, okay?

148
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:41,628
It's okay.

149
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,214
I can't always be there for you.

150
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:46,716
You can't?

151
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:50,637
You can't?

152
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,848
I'm not joking.

153
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:59,187
You played a trick
on Chang Chien-yuan.
It's dangerous.

154
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,566
I don't agree
with doing it this way either.

155
00:08:04,985 --> 00:08:06,987
What do you mean?

156
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:09,572
Attacking people online,
sneaking shots.

157
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:12,450
I don't accept that.

158
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:14,618
I'm giving them
a taste of their own medicine.

159
00:08:14,619 --> 00:08:16,538
So we're no different
from them.

160
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:20,207
We've been working so hard,
and he smeared our reputation.

161
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:22,668
We need to hit them back.

162
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:24,671
I want to defeat them
fair and square.

163
00:08:25,714 --> 00:08:28,008
Oh, my! You're selfish!

164
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:35,139
You only care
about your justice.

165
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,641
What about the others?

166
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:42,688
Yu-li worked so hard
to overcome her fear of fire.

167
00:08:42,689 --> 00:08:44,857
Chin-nan sucked it up
and changed his bad temper

168
00:08:44,858 --> 00:08:46,650
in front of those
difficult customers.

169
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:49,069
But customers don't care.

170
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:52,323
When they see one-star reviews,
they'll ignore our hard work.

171
00:08:52,574 --> 00:08:55,952
But you only care about
your justice and principles.

172
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:57,162
Isn't that selfish?

173
00:08:58,621 --> 00:09:00,080
I'm the manager of Jin Lai Hao.

174
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:02,042
I have the responsibility
to protect my co-workers

175
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:04,294
and defend their blood,
sweat, and tears.

176
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:09,006
Whoever tries to mess
with them, I'll smash it
right back twice as hard.

177
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:11,009
And that's me, Chao Yi-hsuan.

178
00:09:11,134 --> 00:09:12,635
[emotional music playing]

179
00:09:13,803 --> 00:09:16,181
You can go on living
with your principles.

180
00:09:16,306 --> 00:09:19,017
But don't try to turn me
into what you want.

181
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:20,684
That's how I am.

182
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:22,895
I'll work hard
to live life the way I want.

183
00:09:22,896 --> 00:09:25,356
If anybody tries
to hurt someone I love,

184
00:09:25,607 --> 00:09:27,317
I'll give him or her
a hard time.

185
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:31,571
[music continues]

186
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:43,041
How's that?
Are you ready?

187
00:09:46,878 --> 00:09:50,131
I know you're a nice guy,
and very loyal.

188
00:09:54,636 --> 00:09:57,639
And I don't hate you for that.

189
00:10:02,102 --> 00:10:04,062
Our turnover hits a record-high!

190
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:06,106
- [laughs]
- [cheers]

191
00:10:06,231 --> 00:10:07,899
[exclaims]

192
00:10:13,822 --> 00:10:18,158
[Yi-hsuan] <i>I want you
to have some weaknesses
to show that I'm important.</i>

193
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:20,370
- But you are important.
- Really?

194
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:29,920
Why are you
still standing there?

195
00:10:29,921 --> 00:10:32,966
[dramatic music continues]

196
00:10:51,401 --> 00:10:53,861
[journalist] <i>Videos recorded
last night showing the heir
of the leading catering group</i>

197
00:10:53,862 --> 00:10:56,196
<i>assaulting someone
on the street.</i>

198
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:58,782
<i>Such impulsive violence
has once again sent
their stock price tumbling.</i>

199
00:10:58,783 --> 00:11:01,326
<i>A hashtag has already
emerged online calling
for a boycott of Chang Xin,</i>

200
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:05,248
<i>and some consumers
are threatening to refuse
to dine in their restaurants.</i>

201
00:11:09,878 --> 00:11:11,254
What are you doing?

202
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:15,717
What the hell?
You just won't listen!

203
00:11:17,093 --> 00:11:18,970
Didn't I tell you

204
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:20,972
that you represent the company?

205
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:23,308
Do everything carefully.

206
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:27,812
Do you know how much
our stock price has plummeted?

207
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:30,314
When our shareholders find out,
what will they think?

208
00:11:30,315 --> 00:11:32,192
Such a disgrace!

209
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:33,234
Damn!

210
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,946
[sighs]

211
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:40,909
Get out!
I don't want to see you.

212
00:12:09,771 --> 00:12:11,022
Have some tea, sir.

213
00:12:12,357 --> 00:12:13,816
[sighs]

214
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:20,823
[Chang Ta-chin sighs]
All that yelling
made me thirsty.

215
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:27,079
By the way,

216
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:30,458
our performance
has been great lately,
all thanks to you.

217
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:33,795
- I'm flattered.
- [laughs]

218
00:12:36,256 --> 00:12:37,215
But...

219
00:12:39,217 --> 00:12:42,053
I feel like I've got sand
in my eye.

220
00:12:44,389 --> 00:12:46,224
I need someone to get it out.

221
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:51,980
What do you mean, sir?

222
00:12:56,901 --> 00:12:58,235
Jin Lai Hao.

223
00:12:58,236 --> 00:13:00,321
[dramatic music playing]

224
00:13:04,409 --> 00:13:06,536
I'm not sure
what you want me to do, sir.

225
00:13:09,831 --> 00:13:12,959
You've been in this position
for a long time.

226
00:13:13,084 --> 00:13:14,252
With your capability,

227
00:13:14,377 --> 00:13:16,462
I think you should be able
to climb much higher.

228
00:13:18,381 --> 00:13:21,426
It's time to prove
your capability and value.

229
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:30,267
Of course,

230
00:13:30,268 --> 00:13:33,104
it's okay if you
don't want to do it.

231
00:13:33,229 --> 00:13:37,190
Some people would love
to try different jobs.

232
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:40,278
You might just find a place
that fits you better.

233
00:13:43,865 --> 00:13:47,367
I don't want to force anybody.

234
00:13:47,368 --> 00:13:49,287
[suspenseful music playing]

235
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:09,140
[smooth rock music playing]

236
00:14:17,648 --> 00:14:20,151
[singer] <i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

237
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:26,491
[female singer] <i>♪ Ah ♪</i>

238
00:14:27,617 --> 00:14:29,285
<i>♪ Don't stop ♪</i>

239
00:14:30,328 --> 00:14:34,332
[singer] <i>♪ Oh, yeah ♪</i>

240
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:37,585
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

241
00:14:42,632 --> 00:14:43,966
[female singer] <i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

242
00:14:46,511 --> 00:14:47,553
<i>♪ You're too much ♪</i>

243
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:49,889
- [singer] <i>♪ Sex ♪</i>
- [sighs]

244
00:14:56,104 --> 00:14:57,063
[music ends]

245
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:04,070
Hey. We need more fish and beef.

246
00:15:04,195 --> 00:15:07,240
Oh.
I'll make a phone call later.

247
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:12,912
I heard the boss is thinking
about opening a new branch.

248
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,458
Oh, yes.

249
00:15:18,501 --> 00:15:21,295
I've made some new dessert.
Let's try it together.

250
00:15:27,218 --> 00:15:30,096
[smooth rock music playing]

251
00:15:38,646 --> 00:15:40,398
[singer] <i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

252
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,282
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

253
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:55,662
[female singer]
<i>♪ You're too much ♪</i>

254
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:58,374
<i>♪ Oh, yeah ♪</i>

255
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:05,548
[music ends]

256
00:16:08,593 --> 00:16:12,012
Why don't you come in here
to take a closer look
and see it clearly?

257
00:16:12,013 --> 00:16:13,638
No.

258
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:16,475
- What, no? I saw you dribbling.
- Come on.

259
00:16:16,476 --> 00:16:18,102
- Does it taste good?
- [Yu-li] Pretty good.

260
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:19,312
Add some condensed milk.

261
00:16:19,437 --> 00:16:20,980
[Feng] Let me try it.

262
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:25,485
[smooth rock music playing]

263
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,617
[Feng] It's no use.

264
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:36,787
You've watched too many movies.

265
00:16:37,038 --> 00:16:39,457
You aren't burned.
What's the icy water for?

266
00:16:41,292 --> 00:16:42,542
Are you in love with Yu-li?

267
00:16:42,543 --> 00:16:44,587
- [whimsical music playing]
- Hey!

268
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:48,173
What are you talking about?
I'm in love with her?

269
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:50,300
It's impossible.
Don't talk nonsense!

270
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:51,761
Come on. Admit it.

271
00:16:52,011 --> 00:16:53,720
I was young once,
and I've been in love.

272
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:56,349
I know that feeling.
You can't hide it. I mean it.

273
00:16:57,558 --> 00:17:00,436
You're only at the first stage.
It's just the beginning.

274
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:04,815
When you've reached
the middle stage, the symptoms
will get worse, you know.

275
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:08,319
What will happen
in the middle stage?

276
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:10,195
The middle stage?

277
00:17:10,196 --> 00:17:15,659
In the middle stage,
everything you see, think about,

278
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:20,498
hear, say, and dwell on
will only be your lover.

279
00:17:24,085 --> 00:17:26,546
Don't worry.
That won't happen.

280
00:17:28,256 --> 00:17:30,049
Are you really
not in love with Yu-li?

281
00:17:30,508 --> 00:17:31,675
Huh?

282
00:17:31,676 --> 00:17:33,761
No? Huh?

283
00:17:34,845 --> 00:17:36,347
Come on.

284
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:38,515
This is my type.

285
00:17:38,516 --> 00:17:41,519
[whimsical music playing]

286
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:47,525
That's your type?
For real?

287
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:48,692
Yeah.

288
00:17:48,693 --> 00:17:50,820
Okay. That's it.

289
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,530
If you say so.

290
00:17:53,531 --> 00:17:54,532
Fine.

291
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,535
Poor boy.

292
00:17:57,660 --> 00:18:00,288
You're lying to yourself.
Oh, my.

293
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:02,622
Poor boy.

294
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:04,375
[Feng] Poor guy.

295
00:18:05,376 --> 00:18:06,586
[scoffs]

296
00:18:06,711 --> 00:18:10,089
You idiot! There's no way
I'm in love with Yu-li.

297
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:16,804
[music continues]

298
00:18:21,559 --> 00:18:23,310
[woman] <i>Hello.</i>

299
00:18:23,311 --> 00:18:25,229
<i>Your profile says
you work at a restaurant.</i>

300
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:27,148
<i>Are you good at cooking?</i>

301
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:30,650
[Chin-nan] <i>Of course.</i>

302
00:18:30,651 --> 00:18:34,572
<i>I'm not only good at cooking,
but also good at other things.</i>

303
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:37,742
YOUR MATCH HAS LEFT
THE CHATROOM.

304
00:18:38,576 --> 00:18:39,910
YOU AND SUE MATCHED!

305
00:18:40,161 --> 00:18:41,828
[Chin-nan] <i>Hi. Shall we go
jogging together?</i>

306
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:43,581
HELLO.

307
00:18:43,706 --> 00:18:45,416
[Chin-nan] <i>Why don't you
come to my place
and see for yourself?</i>

308
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:47,709
<i>You're cute,
the cutest girl in the world.</i>

309
00:18:47,710 --> 00:18:49,587
YOUR MATCH
HAS LEFT THE CHATROOM.
YOU HAVE NO OTHER MATCHES.

310
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:58,471
CHIN-NAN: WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

311
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:02,642
[Chin-nan] <i>Hey.</i>

312
00:19:05,478 --> 00:19:06,520
[woman] <i>Hey, your ass.</i>

313
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:12,735
[Chin-nan] <i>I have a cute ass.</i>

314
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:19,325
[woman] <i>Oh.</i>

315
00:19:25,706 --> 00:19:27,917
[whimsical music playing]

316
00:19:35,758 --> 00:19:36,842
What the hell?

317
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:41,931
I'm thinking about nothing
but Yu-li. Nothing but Yu-li.

318
00:19:42,223 --> 00:19:45,643
Yu-li is too tall and big
to fit in my brain.

319
00:19:45,768 --> 00:19:47,852
[angelic music playing]

320
00:19:47,853 --> 00:19:49,605
[music winds down]

321
00:19:52,316 --> 00:19:53,858
Listen.

322
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:55,319
This is my type.

323
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:01,659
A sweet, sexy and cute girl.

324
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:06,372
Yu-li can't compete with you.

325
00:20:06,497 --> 00:20:08,581
My brain isn't full of shit.

326
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:10,334
[angelic music playing]

327
00:20:12,837 --> 00:20:14,587
[music winds down]

328
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:15,548
[grunts]

329
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:22,388
Yu-li.
(Hello.)

330
00:20:25,433 --> 00:20:26,350
Have a seat.

331
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:27,393
Yu-li.
(Thanks.)

332
00:20:27,518 --> 00:20:29,520
[whimsical music playing]

333
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:31,897
Yu-li, Yu-li.
(I'm late.)

334
00:20:32,022 --> 00:20:35,276
Yu-li, Yu-li, Yu-li.
(I'm really sorry.)

335
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:43,784
Yu-li, Yu-li, Yu-li, Yu-li.
(You look better in person.)

336
00:20:45,578 --> 00:20:46,954
[laughs]

337
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:52,460
Everything you see,

338
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:54,795
think about,

339
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:56,756
hear...

340
00:20:56,881 --> 00:20:58,716
[woman] Yu-li, Yu-li...

341
00:20:58,841 --> 00:21:00,551
will only be your lover.

342
00:21:03,888 --> 00:21:05,055
Are you in love with me?

343
00:21:13,564 --> 00:21:15,858
[upbeat music playing]

344
00:21:17,401 --> 00:21:20,987
[singer] <i>♪ I have no choice ♪</i>

345
00:21:20,988 --> 00:21:22,947
<i>♪ If I knew ♪</i>

346
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:28,661
<i>♪ You didn't truly love me ♪</i>

347
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:33,000
<i>♪ I wouldn't have fallen
In love with you so easily ♪</i>

348
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:36,711
<i>♪ If you truly love me ♪</i>

349
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:41,425
<i>♪ Why did you leave
Without telling me? ♪</i>

350
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:43,052
<i>♪ But now ♪</i>

351
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:48,432
<i>♪ I can do nothing
But blame myself ♪</i>

352
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:50,433
<i>♪ I have no choice ♪</i>

353
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:55,314
<i>♪ I'm missing you so much ♪</i>

354
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:57,649
<i>♪ I have no choice ♪</i>

355
00:21:57,650 --> 00:22:02,071
<i>♪ I'm really
in love with you ♪</i>

356
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:03,948
<i>♪ I have no choice ♪</i>

357
00:22:04,073 --> 00:22:08,828
<i>♪ All I can do is put away ♪</i>

358
00:22:08,953 --> 00:22:10,788
<i>♪ My love for you in secret ♪</i>

359
00:22:10,913 --> 00:22:15,835
<i>♪ And bury it in my heart ♪</i>

360
00:22:17,628 --> 00:22:18,712
[chuckles]

361
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:23,008
I'm in love with my best pal.

362
00:22:24,677 --> 00:22:27,471
I'm in love with my best pal.

363
00:22:28,472 --> 00:22:30,808
I'm in love with my best pal.

364
00:22:30,933 --> 00:22:32,351
[dramatic music playing]

365
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:36,021
I'm in love with my best pal!

366
00:22:37,064 --> 00:22:41,651
I'm in love with my best pal!

367
00:22:41,652 --> 00:22:43,486
My boy!

368
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:45,656
My love!

369
00:22:45,781 --> 00:22:47,700
My boy love!

370
00:22:47,825 --> 00:22:50,035
[cats screeching]

371
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:53,122
[music ends]

372
00:23:10,973 --> 00:23:13,058
There's something
I can't figure out.

373
00:23:14,476 --> 00:23:19,690
I think a dad teaching his son
is perfectly reasonable.

374
00:23:21,525 --> 00:23:23,527
But why?

375
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:27,698
Why would he have to do it
in front of an outsider?

376
00:23:36,999 --> 00:23:38,626
My dad likes you so much.

377
00:23:40,127 --> 00:23:42,963
Would he make you his successor?

378
00:23:47,801 --> 00:23:48,844
[sighs]

379
00:23:53,557 --> 00:23:55,726
I have work to do.
Please get up.

380
00:24:05,069 --> 00:24:06,445
Oh, I see.

381
00:24:08,781 --> 00:24:11,825
You knew I'd be
doing this, right?

382
00:24:16,121 --> 00:24:17,081
Fine.

383
00:24:18,999 --> 00:24:20,250
Accepted.

384
00:24:20,501 --> 00:24:23,795
Help me get back to where I was.

385
00:24:23,796 --> 00:24:26,465
Then, however you want to use me
is up to you, okay?

386
00:24:26,590 --> 00:24:28,174
I'm not in love with you
or using you.

387
00:24:28,175 --> 00:24:29,634
It's your wishful thinking.

388
00:24:29,635 --> 00:24:31,844
Why? Why aren't you
in love with me?

389
00:24:31,845 --> 00:24:33,806
What are you doing? Let go.
What are you doing?

390
00:24:33,931 --> 00:24:35,014
Let go!

391
00:24:35,015 --> 00:24:37,476
What do you want? Let go!

392
00:24:43,524 --> 00:24:44,942
Do you know what you're doing?

393
00:24:45,067 --> 00:24:47,528
[panting]

394
00:24:52,116 --> 00:24:55,119
[dramatic music playing]

395
00:25:01,291 --> 00:25:02,917
I'm an outsider.

396
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:04,836
If I don't do my job well,
I'll get fired.

397
00:25:04,837 --> 00:25:07,798
But you're your dad's son.
His blood flows in you.

398
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:11,135
As long as you work hard enough,
he'll see. Don't you understand?

399
00:25:15,806 --> 00:25:17,224
I've been working hard.

400
00:25:19,935 --> 00:25:22,771
I have always been
working so hard.

401
00:25:30,863 --> 00:25:33,032
[music continues]

402
00:25:40,164 --> 00:25:41,123
Damn!

403
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:45,210
I'm sorry.

404
00:25:58,057 --> 00:25:59,183
[sighs]

405
00:26:15,074 --> 00:26:17,534
LU-YUNG: I'M GONNA TAKE
A DAY OFF TOMORROW.

406
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:19,786
PLEASE TAKE CARE
OF THE RESTAURANT.

407
00:26:19,787 --> 00:26:21,704
CHIN-NAN: YES, SIR.

408
00:26:21,705 --> 00:26:23,332
YU-LI: NO PROBLEM.

409
00:26:32,883 --> 00:26:36,345
YI-HSUAN: WHY DOES BOSS
TAKE A DAY OFF EVERY FEW MONTHS?

410
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:39,264
YU-LI: I DON'T KNOW.

411
00:26:39,389 --> 00:26:42,601
GOING TO AN UNKNOWN
MYSTERIOUS PLACE?

412
00:26:46,814 --> 00:26:49,107
What does he have to do?

413
00:26:49,108 --> 00:26:50,317
And he doesn't tell us.

414
00:26:52,069 --> 00:26:54,696
Our boss is indeed
a mysterious guy.

415
00:26:59,201 --> 00:27:02,246
It's a weekday tomorrow.
You won't need me, will you?

416
00:27:03,914 --> 00:27:06,375
We never need you, you know.
[chuckles]

417
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:07,417
Where are you going?

418
00:27:09,336 --> 00:27:13,924
I'm going to explore
that unknown mysterious place.

419
00:27:15,259 --> 00:27:17,136
- You're scary.
- [squeals]

420
00:27:17,261 --> 00:27:21,097
What are you doing to our boss?
You bad girl. Bad girl.

421
00:27:21,098 --> 00:27:23,851
[upbeat music playing]

422
00:27:30,274 --> 00:27:31,358
What are you doing here?

423
00:27:31,984 --> 00:27:33,026
Where are you going?

424
00:27:34,444 --> 00:27:36,320
I'm your manager, right?

425
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:38,323
Why don't you tell me
where you're going?

426
00:27:43,078 --> 00:27:45,247
But this is my personal time.

427
00:27:45,873 --> 00:27:47,833
We're a team.

428
00:27:47,958 --> 00:27:49,418
You can share
everything with me.

429
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:51,128
I can help you.

430
00:27:52,713 --> 00:27:53,797
But it's far away.

431
00:27:55,132 --> 00:27:56,633
Are you coming with me?

432
00:27:56,758 --> 00:27:57,843
Sure.

433
00:27:59,970 --> 00:28:01,304
[chuckles]

434
00:28:01,305 --> 00:28:02,264
Let's go.

435
00:28:08,687 --> 00:28:10,898
[birds chirping]

436
00:28:11,690 --> 00:28:13,192
[soft music playing]

437
00:28:14,902 --> 00:28:16,444
[indistinct speaking]

438
00:28:16,445 --> 00:28:20,699
[Yi-hsuan] <i>Our boss said
he was going back to Tainan.</i>

439
00:28:20,824 --> 00:28:23,994
<i>He goes back home
every few months.</i>

440
00:28:25,204 --> 00:28:29,124
<i>On the way,
he told me his past,</i>

441
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:33,503
<i>including his life
with his dad,</i>

442
00:28:33,754 --> 00:28:35,881
<i>how the original
Jin Lai Hao started</i>

443
00:28:36,924 --> 00:28:40,928
<i>and how it all began.</i>

444
00:28:49,978 --> 00:28:51,979
<i>Defeating Chang Da-chin</i>

445
00:28:51,980 --> 00:28:54,232
<i>and upholding his dad's
original culinary vision</i>

446
00:28:54,233 --> 00:28:56,526
<i>have become
his most important mission.</i>

447
00:29:00,989 --> 00:29:03,158
<i>But to turn things around,</i>

448
00:29:03,283 --> 00:29:05,117
<i>what he needs most</i>

449
00:29:05,118 --> 00:29:06,536
<i>is the person
who knows the truth</i>

450
00:29:06,787 --> 00:29:08,120
<i>about what happened
back then.</i>

451
00:29:08,121 --> 00:29:10,457
[music continues]

452
00:29:16,171 --> 00:29:19,216
[birds chirping]

453
00:29:37,901 --> 00:29:39,152
I think there's nobody home.

454
00:29:41,071 --> 00:29:42,155
Mr. Wang?

455
00:29:44,908 --> 00:29:46,201
Mr. Wang?

456
00:29:47,244 --> 00:29:48,370
Isn't he home?

457
00:29:50,122 --> 00:29:51,081
[Lu-yung] Mr. Wang?

458
00:29:52,416 --> 00:29:53,417
[sighs]

459
00:30:00,132 --> 00:30:02,050
[Officer Wang]
I quit the police long ago.

460
00:30:03,343 --> 00:30:06,805
I know I let you down,
but I can't help you.

461
00:30:06,930 --> 00:30:08,348
I want you to tell the truth.

462
00:30:09,891 --> 00:30:12,060
Only you can help punish
the real murderer.

463
00:30:14,271 --> 00:30:15,772
Leave me alone.

464
00:30:15,897 --> 00:30:17,566
You're here every few months,
which bothers me.

465
00:30:18,608 --> 00:30:19,984
Wait...

466
00:30:19,985 --> 00:30:21,987
[Officer Wang]
Go away. Go home now.

467
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:26,283
[sighs]

468
00:30:29,828 --> 00:30:31,163
One day, I'll convince him.

469
00:30:34,166 --> 00:30:35,333
[sighs]

470
00:30:35,334 --> 00:30:38,378
[dramatic music playing]

471
00:30:44,343 --> 00:30:45,594
I promise you.

472
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:47,470
I'll resume
the investigation, okay?

473
00:30:47,471 --> 00:30:49,598
[thunder rumbling]

474
00:30:51,933 --> 00:30:53,852
This hit-and-run driver

475
00:30:53,977 --> 00:30:56,355
was having dinner
when the car accident happened.

476
00:30:56,480 --> 00:30:58,857
He was far away
from the crime scene.

477
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:06,323
[breathes heavily]

478
00:31:14,498 --> 00:31:17,376
[police chief] Wang, leave it.

479
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:20,212
Why don't you think about

480
00:31:20,337 --> 00:31:23,048
what you should be
thinking about?

481
00:31:28,011 --> 00:31:31,347
But Chief, we are policemen.

482
00:31:31,348 --> 00:31:33,224
How can we do such things?

483
00:31:33,225 --> 00:31:36,478
Chang Da-chin is more powerful
than any one of us, understand?

484
00:31:42,275 --> 00:31:45,112
We all have our families
to support, okay?

485
00:31:50,367 --> 00:31:51,368
[sighs]

486
00:31:51,493 --> 00:31:53,578
[insects trilling]

487
00:32:06,967 --> 00:32:08,135
Welcome to my childhood home.

488
00:32:09,678 --> 00:32:12,430
You come back
to clean up regularly?

489
00:32:12,431 --> 00:32:15,433
[Lu-yung] Yeah, about every
three or four months.

490
00:32:15,434 --> 00:32:17,269
[Yi-hsuan] What about
your dad's Jin Lai Hao?

491
00:32:18,937 --> 00:32:20,062
[Lu-yung]
Right next to the alley.

492
00:32:20,063 --> 00:32:21,481
But it was torn down.

493
00:32:31,241 --> 00:32:32,200
Are you hungry?

494
00:32:33,743 --> 00:32:35,454
<i>I'll make you
the best fried rice.</i>

495
00:32:35,579 --> 00:32:38,415
- Are you a cook?
- [Lu-yung] Me?

496
00:32:38,540 --> 00:32:39,958
I'm my dad's assistant.

497
00:32:43,587 --> 00:32:44,588
[camera clicks]

498
00:32:46,173 --> 00:32:47,507
[Lu-yung] I'm going
upstairs to clean up.

499
00:32:49,092 --> 00:32:50,969
I'll make us something to eat.

500
00:32:51,094 --> 00:32:52,094
[camera clicks]

501
00:32:52,095 --> 00:32:53,345
Are you alright?

502
00:32:53,346 --> 00:32:55,640
[pendulum clock chiming]

503
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:57,309
[camera clicks]

504
00:32:57,434 --> 00:32:59,351
Good. I'm going upstairs.

505
00:32:59,352 --> 00:33:01,730
[tense music playing]

506
00:33:17,162 --> 00:33:20,207
[suspenseful music playing]

507
00:33:30,550 --> 00:33:31,593
[glass breaks]

508
00:33:34,221 --> 00:33:35,514
[Lu-yung] Yi-hsuan?

509
00:33:41,520 --> 00:33:43,480
[thunder rumbling]

510
00:33:45,023 --> 00:33:45,857
What's wrong?

511
00:33:54,824 --> 00:33:56,993
It's raining heavily.

512
00:33:57,118 --> 00:33:59,411
We'll leave
when it slows down a bit.

513
00:33:59,412 --> 00:34:00,789
Let's eat something.

514
00:34:02,624 --> 00:34:04,334
[Yi-hsuan] When I was little,

515
00:34:05,544 --> 00:34:07,420
you made me fried rice.

516
00:34:08,797 --> 00:34:11,132
[dramatic music playing]

517
00:34:15,637 --> 00:34:17,222
[Lu-yung] <i>I'll make you
the best fried rice.</i>

518
00:34:17,347 --> 00:34:18,723
Do you eat green onions?

519
00:34:18,848 --> 00:34:21,685
Okay. Are you a cook?

520
00:34:21,810 --> 00:34:23,395
Me?

521
00:34:23,520 --> 00:34:25,355
I'm my dad's assistant.

522
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:26,689
Our restaurant is opening soon.

523
00:34:26,690 --> 00:34:28,525
- [camera clicks]
- He's developing a new dish.

524
00:34:29,192 --> 00:34:31,361
- What dish?
- Braised pork knuckles.

525
00:34:31,486 --> 00:34:32,821
They're cooking now.

526
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:35,365
The most challenging part is
to remove the hair.

527
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:36,866
How do you know?

528
00:34:37,534 --> 00:34:40,078
[Young Yi-hsuan] Just look it up
online and you'll see.

529
00:34:40,328 --> 00:34:41,787
Oh...

530
00:34:41,788 --> 00:34:43,039
Do you want to help me?

531
00:34:43,164 --> 00:34:45,542
No. All I want is to eat them.

532
00:34:45,667 --> 00:34:47,460
[Lu-yung laughs] Fine.

533
00:34:51,089 --> 00:34:52,548
[groans]

534
00:34:52,549 --> 00:34:54,092
What's wrong?

535
00:34:54,217 --> 00:34:55,426
[Yi-hsuan] I got burned.

536
00:34:55,427 --> 00:34:57,095
Burned? Come here.

537
00:34:58,430 --> 00:34:59,556
Let me see.

538
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:01,600
Are you alright?

539
00:35:02,726 --> 00:35:04,436
It hurts slightly.

540
00:35:04,561 --> 00:35:07,272
But it's okay.
It'll be fine in a bit.

541
00:35:07,397 --> 00:35:08,356
Are you really alright?

542
00:35:10,609 --> 00:35:11,610
Here.

543
00:35:11,735 --> 00:35:13,612
My super delicious fried rice.

544
00:35:14,738 --> 00:35:16,072
[Yi-hsuan] So cute!

545
00:35:16,197 --> 00:35:17,324
[Lu-yung chuckles]

546
00:35:18,408 --> 00:35:19,701
Here, Lu-yung, a gift for you.

547
00:35:23,580 --> 00:35:24,788
Thank you.

548
00:35:24,789 --> 00:35:27,334
- Here goes.
- Mm-hmm.

549
00:35:30,837 --> 00:35:32,630
[Lu-yung] Does it taste good?

550
00:35:32,631 --> 00:35:33,672
Yeah.

551
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:35,300
[chuckles]

552
00:35:39,262 --> 00:35:42,265
[dramatic music playing]

553
00:35:50,231 --> 00:35:51,690
You're that little girl?

554
00:35:51,691 --> 00:35:53,318
So, we knew each other long ago.

555
00:35:58,365 --> 00:35:59,407
[sighs]

556
00:36:02,494 --> 00:36:03,828
I remember...

557
00:36:07,207 --> 00:36:09,292
I came here with my mom.

558
00:36:18,301 --> 00:36:19,636
Do you remember her?

559
00:36:22,972 --> 00:36:25,308
[Lu-yung] <i>I remember
she was my dad's co-worker,</i>

560
00:36:25,433 --> 00:36:27,185
<i>an elegant lady.</i>

561
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:34,734
Is that all?

562
00:36:36,820 --> 00:36:38,238
[thunder rumbling]

563
00:36:39,823 --> 00:36:40,824
[scoffs]

564
00:36:41,991 --> 00:36:43,368
[sniffles]

565
00:36:44,869 --> 00:36:46,870
[sobbing]

566
00:36:46,871 --> 00:36:51,000
I even remember
what your dad looked like.

567
00:36:51,251 --> 00:36:54,170
But I really can't remember
what my mom looked like.

568
00:36:54,295 --> 00:36:57,340
[dramatic music playing]

569
00:37:01,845 --> 00:37:02,886
[crying] If...

570
00:37:02,887 --> 00:37:05,890
If one day, she comes back,

571
00:37:06,808 --> 00:37:09,227
will I not recognize her?

572
00:37:10,854 --> 00:37:12,605
[sobbing]

573
00:37:15,567 --> 00:37:16,526
Come on.

574
00:37:19,279 --> 00:37:20,321
It's alright.

575
00:37:23,408 --> 00:37:24,868
I'll be right here with you.

576
00:37:28,288 --> 00:37:29,247
It's alright.

577
00:37:31,332 --> 00:37:32,917
[thunder rumbling]

578
00:37:43,344 --> 00:37:45,305
[rain pattering]

579
00:37:46,848 --> 00:37:48,641
[birds chirping]

580
00:37:52,729 --> 00:37:55,774
[soft music playing]

581
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:15,668
[utensils clattering]

582
00:38:23,051 --> 00:38:24,010
[Yi-hsuan] Hi.

583
00:38:25,011 --> 00:38:25,970
You're up.

584
00:38:27,472 --> 00:38:29,932
I was going to wake you up
when I finished cooking.

585
00:38:29,933 --> 00:38:31,975
You didn't eat anything
yesterday.

586
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:33,686
I wanted to make you
some fried rice.

587
00:38:42,987 --> 00:38:44,823
You must be hungry. Eat up.

588
00:38:53,873 --> 00:38:55,875
How is it? Does it taste good?

589
00:38:59,128 --> 00:39:00,129
Very tasty.

590
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:12,141
[chuckling]

591
00:39:18,690 --> 00:39:21,109
[birds chirping]

592
00:39:25,113 --> 00:39:27,490
[soft music playing]

593
00:40:10,033 --> 00:40:12,201
[birds chirping]

594
00:40:20,043 --> 00:40:22,086
- [upbeat music playing]
- [phone chimes]

595
00:40:24,714 --> 00:40:25,715
How's this one?

596
00:40:29,510 --> 00:40:31,179
Not bad. Looks good.

597
00:40:32,931 --> 00:40:34,849
Feng, what do you think?

598
00:40:36,059 --> 00:40:37,727
- Ask her out.
- [laughs]

599
00:40:37,852 --> 00:40:39,729
Invite her out for drinks.

600
00:40:39,854 --> 00:40:41,064
- Are you finished, Feng?
- Yeah.

601
00:40:41,189 --> 00:40:43,649
- I'll clean up for you.
- Thank you.

602
00:40:43,650 --> 00:40:45,401
You're welcome.

603
00:40:45,526 --> 00:40:46,611
[phone chimes]

604
00:40:47,862 --> 00:40:49,113
[Yu-li] Keep swiping.

605
00:40:49,238 --> 00:40:52,074
See if you can get someone
even hotter.

606
00:40:52,075 --> 00:40:53,826
[laughing]

607
00:40:57,705 --> 00:40:59,207
You idiot. You idiot.

608
00:40:59,457 --> 00:41:01,041
She's smarter than you.

609
00:41:01,042 --> 00:41:02,919
Don't try to play
mind games with her.

610
00:41:03,044 --> 00:41:05,755
You won't win, you know?

611
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:07,632
Love is simple.

612
00:41:08,925 --> 00:41:11,594
Be genuine and sincere,
and just go for it.

613
00:41:11,719 --> 00:41:14,222
It's either yes or no.

614
00:41:14,472 --> 00:41:15,931
[woman moaning]

615
00:41:15,932 --> 00:41:18,601
Damn, scammed again.
Another porn.

616
00:41:20,728 --> 00:41:22,230
[telephone ringing]

617
00:41:27,527 --> 00:41:28,987
Hello? This is Jin Lai Hao.

618
00:41:32,615 --> 00:41:33,782
[door opens]

619
00:41:33,783 --> 00:41:34,993
Huh?

620
00:41:35,702 --> 00:41:36,661
Say it again?

621
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,166
[Lu-yung] Yeah, I see.

622
00:41:43,876 --> 00:41:44,836
Okay.

623
00:41:46,587 --> 00:41:48,171
Thank you.

624
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:50,174
How was it?
What did the lawyer say?

625
00:41:52,719 --> 00:41:54,137
He said there's nothing
we can do.

626
00:41:56,055 --> 00:41:59,642
But when we signed the contract,
we added a clause stating that

627
00:41:59,767 --> 00:42:01,686
if the landlord wants
an early termination,

628
00:42:01,811 --> 00:42:03,688
she's responsible for our losses
in decoration costs.

629
00:42:03,813 --> 00:42:05,815
- Is she okay with that?
- [Chin-nan] She's right.

630
00:42:07,567 --> 00:42:09,985
I think there's another business
wanting to rent the storefront.

631
00:42:09,986 --> 00:42:11,320
Damn! It's not right.

632
00:42:11,571 --> 00:42:13,280
We signed a three-year contract.

633
00:42:13,281 --> 00:42:15,991
Now we have to move
just because she told us to?

634
00:42:15,992 --> 00:42:18,285
We have no choice.
The landlord owns the place.

635
00:42:18,286 --> 00:42:21,289
She has the right
to decide who she leases it to.

636
00:42:22,165 --> 00:42:24,125
We don't own a place.

637
00:42:25,585 --> 00:42:27,295
That's the sad reality.

638
00:42:29,088 --> 00:42:31,882
Damn! Son of a bitch!

639
00:42:31,883 --> 00:42:33,051
[door opens]

640
00:42:35,678 --> 00:42:37,555
[landlord] Excuse me.

641
00:42:38,765 --> 00:42:40,308
It's nothing.

642
00:42:40,558 --> 00:42:42,768
I just brought the new owner
to take a look at the place.

643
00:42:42,769 --> 00:42:43,728
New owner?

644
00:42:43,853 --> 00:42:45,855
Yeah, our buyer.

645
00:42:46,939 --> 00:42:48,774
She's interested
in your equipment.

646
00:42:48,775 --> 00:42:50,233
Don't you have
the equipment here?

647
00:42:50,234 --> 00:42:51,778
Why don't you talk to her?

648
00:42:53,071 --> 00:42:55,947
I'll leave you to it.
I've got to go.

649
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:57,075
Take your time.

650
00:42:57,200 --> 00:42:58,700
[chuckles]

651
00:42:58,701 --> 00:43:01,829
[suspenseful music playing]

652
00:43:15,384 --> 00:43:18,596
[credits music playing]
